= env-does-not-repair-a-poisoned-session
f libexec/mux-env_lib
t mux-wire
# THE WHOLE FAULT. An agent-less attach records `-NAME`, which MASKS the server
# global, so there is no lower layer to fall back on and every pane created
# afterwards starts without the pointer. Measured on a real box: every agent
# pane running with no SSH_AUTH_SOCK, git push failing in every repo, and the
# box otherwise healthy.
#
# THE WRITE ITSELF IS THE ANCHOR, not the dry-run guard above it: that guard
# appears in both the write and the clear branches, so the corpus correctly
# refused it as ambiguous.
-           tm set-environment -t "$_eas" \
+           true \
