= open-classes-the-wrong-window
f libexec/mux-window_lib
t mux-agent
# A CLASS RECORDED AGAINST THE WRONG PANE is this package's signature
# failure: plausible, wrong and silent. Dropping the window from the target
# sets it on whatever window the session happens to have current, which with
# `-d` is NOT the one just created, so the worker stays `human` (refused to
# every sender) while some other pane silently becomes agent-controlled.
-     _mwt set-option -p -t "=$_mwsess:$_mwidx" \
+     _mwt set-option -p -t "=$_mwsess" \
