= window-human-verb-detaches
f libexec/mux-window
t mux-window
# THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN THE TWO PRESENTERS. `mux window` is what a
# HUMAN types, so it creates AND goes there; `mux agent open` is what a
# program calls, so it creates detached. Flip the engine's switch argument
# and the human gets a window made somewhere they are not, which is the
# mirror of the defect vicus's hand-rolled copy had in the other direction.
-   "$_cmd" "$_ctl" "$_attn" 1 || _wrc=$?
+   "$_cmd" "$_ctl" "$_attn" 0 || _wrc=$?
