= class-relax-needs-a-human
f libexec/mux-agent
t mux-agent
# THE SECURITY-RELEVANT HALF OF R3. A machine may move a pane TOWARD the
# human freely, because that only removes its own permission and adds the
# human's sight of it; the reverse GRANTS, and relaxing a pane to `agent` is
# precisely the laundering move (promote a human's pane, then send into it
# wherever a `control:agent` grant is in force).
#
# THE GATE IS ORGANISATIONAL and the source says so: an agent can allocate a
# pty and can call `tmux set-option` directly today. What it buys is that the
# dangerous direction stops being the easy one, which is exactly what this
# record protects: with the gate gone, relaxing is a plain machine call.
-       if [ ! -t 0 ] || [ -z "$_clyes" ]; then
+       if false; then
